    "body": "Proves a continuous, onto, finite-to-one map from the literal σₖ ordinary hull to its full solenoid. The map intertwines translation and inflation. Every preimage of the zero history is inflation-periodic.\n\n## Work shown\n\n### Assumptions and hypotheses\n\nThe literal family and Perron lengths are those of PR #639. The factor is constructed for every integer k ≥ 1. The common-tile endpoint at k ≥ 2 uses the legal-patch transfer from #641 and assumes the three exact window agreements it consumes.\n\n### Derivation / reduction\n\nThe images locate parents of types 1 and 2 using the tile 2 and consecutive tiles 00. These parents determine the remaining parents of type 0. Inflation is closed, and exact recurrence makes its image dense. The family's irreducible incidence polynomial then supplies the stable contraction.\n\nAt each desubstitution depth, equal solenoid coordinates bound the integer difference of the two lifts. Relative to a reference member of the fibre, this bounds the possible small windows by one finite collection. Inflation of those windows distinguishes any prescribed finite set of distinct tilings. For surjectivity, propagate cube lifts of deep coordinates forward. Their stable parts vanish at each fixed depth, so the zero orbit is dense. Compactness of the ordinary hull makes the image closed, and the seam 1.1 realizes to zero.\n\nEach hull orbit is dense, so continuous equivariant maps into the same time-normalized solenoid have identical fibres. The proof note identifies the published target and gives the remaining analytic obligations. [Derivation](docs/c4-family-solenoid-factor-2026-11-21.md)\n\n### Evidence and replay\n\nLean 4.34.0-rc2 built the family, its controls and the realization models. The scoped audit checked 35 endpoint types and 1,053 declarations across 23 modules, with 70 refusal controls. It accepted only the standard Lean axioms. The hosted gate replays the source closure with `tools/check_c4_parameter_family.sh`. The continuity dependencies reused from #627 are source-identical to `23ffa29a0bbdcd97ea9bb7c2768a11f3f9b1bce8`.\n\n### Negative controls\n\nThe literal vector (1/2, 0, 1/2) has a nonzero class in the torus and maps to the class of (1, 1, 0). The audit therefore checks failure of injectivity of the single-torus endomorphism for every k ≥ 1. Its endpoint matcher rejects missing names and declarations of the wrong type.\n\n### Non-claims / remaining gaps\n\nLean still needs the common-shift witnesses for pairs with equal images over zero and the coincidence-rank implication for the invariant-measure L² spectrum. The comparison with the published maximal equicontinuous factor uses a written target identification. The family already has a written spectral proof using the published criterion. Universal BH, residual A1′ and C4 are separate research obligations.",
    "title": "Prove the finite-to-one σₖ solenoid realization",
