    "body": "Continue the geometric proof after #639. For every `k ≥ 2`, the literal swap certificate now gives dense eventual coincidence on the open overlap of any two legal patches sharing a tile. [Proof and source decision](docs/c4-family-legal-coincidence-2026-11-21.md)\n\n## Work shown\n\n### Assumptions and hypotheses\n\nThe transfer uses the literal periodic test tiling, a dense coincidence set for one shift irrational relative to its period, and a level at which every letter occurs in every image. The family supplies all three inputs. The final periodic-fibre theorem takes injective inflation, an inflation semiconjugacy with finite fibres, and the closed-origin witnesses for same-fibre pairs.\n\n### Derivation / reduction\n\n- At a common depth, coverage by common tiles gives a transitive local relation. Taking the interior of the whole covered region preserves shared descendant seams.\n- The closure of the coincidence set for a displacement is invariant under the generator and period. The irrational ratio makes their subgroup dense. A single common tile in two translated legal embeddings then gives dense coincidence on their open overlap.\n- Equal closed origin patches give local agreement, including at seams. The two-point witnesses give a common tile for the inflation-periodic partners after advancing to a common multiple of their periods. Finite-fibre lifting applies this argument to all pairs in the fibre of the constructed inflation-periodic tiling under the stated factor hypotheses.\n\n### Evidence and replay\n\nLean 4.34.0-rc2 built the scoped targets at head `e5d84d054a0a1b29d7a25d2bc13d05974b96c4bb`, whose tree `c8dfd3a1bc13709184880d83939a987156893a6e` matches the tested local tree. The family audit checked 753 declarations across 13 owned modules, 664 theorem declarations, 24 endpoint types, and 48 refusal controls. Its axiom closure used standard Lean axioms only. The 65 focused tests, proof-bank check, dependency-pin validation, claim-governance audit, and whitespace check passed.\n\n```sh\ncd proof/PscVerif\nlake --no-cache build PscVerif.C4ParameterFamilyTiling PscVerif.C4ParameterFamilyControls PscVerif.UniversalClosureReduction\nlake --no-cache env lean C4ParameterFamilyAudit.lean\n```\n\nThe dedicated hosted workflow also runs the isolated family gate.\n\n### Negative controls\n\nThe Thue–Morse audit places the original midpoint on a child seam. It checks that the common region retains a neighborhood there and that every individual child interior misses the point. The existing finite-factor and wrong-endpoint controls remain in the gate.\n\n### Non-claims / remaining gaps\n\nThe spectral conclusion in Lean still needs the concrete maximal equicontinuous factor, its finite fibres, and the same-fibre witness implication. The measure step is to connect the exclusion of disjoint pairs to coincidence rank one and density of eigenfunctions in the invariant measure's `L²` space. The published Corollary 2 supplies the written family spectral conclusion.",
